{"connection_id": "BC-3c204db8f0b8af01adaa", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.16.26", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "gain world yet lose life", "note": "Jesus asks what profit there is in gaining the world while forfeiting one's life; this gives the commentary's human loss a pointed accounting comparison."}
{"connection_id": "BC-aa8ab3d5403737af21fd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.16.27", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "coming judge repays each by deeds", "note": "The commentary's appointed day brings every person to recompense for work; Jesus says the Son of Man comes in glory and repays each according to what that person has done."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ec9fb69e3f32329c554d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.16.27", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "repay each according to deeds", "note": "The Son of Man comes in glory and repays each person according to conduct; the commentary likewise brings everyone to an appointed day and settles the account by works."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7fdce425fbcec5b5fda2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.18.23", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "a king settles accounts", "note": "The commentary uses an account image for loss and recompense; Jesus begins a kingdom parable with a king settling accounts with servants, then develops how debt and mercy affect the verdict."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6280c1bd40e801e56666", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.18.34", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "forgiven debtor punished for withholding mercy", "note": "The commentary sorts deeds toward punishment or reward; in the parable a servant whose debt was forgiven is handed over after refusing mercy to another, making the treatment of one's neighbor decisive."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6c3246563a12434b4ac1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.23.32", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "evil measure filled", "note": "Jesus tells his opponents to fill up the measure of their ancestors; this makes moral evil accumulate toward judgment like the commentary's bad things piled one on another."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bf85cfc245192eca359a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.24.13", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endure to the end", "note": "The commentary's patience belongs to the people who escape loss; Jesus says the one who endures to the end will be saved, placing perseverance within an apocalyptic warning."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bc05ed6407486caf4f5d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.32", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "all nations; separation", "note": "The commentary describes the final distinction between good and evil; Matthew gathers all nations before the Son of Man, who separates people as a shepherd separates sheep from goats."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a6b6755c8fbb45b41cb2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.32", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "separation of all nations", "note": "The Son of Man gathers the nations and separates people as a shepherd separates sheep from goats; this supplies a scene for the commentary's final sorting of good from bad."}
{"connection_id": "BC-41b34f83ffc3f3610d4a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.35", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "concrete deeds rewarded", "note": "The welcomed people fed the hungry and gave drink to the thirsty; the commentary's righteous deeds gain small, tangible instances used in the final verdict."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f058e0c4824acfbe9323", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.40", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "deeds to the least count as deeds to the king", "note": "The commentary says deeds determine the account; Matthew makes acts of care toward the least of the king's siblings count as acts done to the king, giving the judgment criterion a concrete social face."}
{"connection_id": "BC-19a86340046765cf798a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.40", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "act for the least counted for the king", "note": "The king says deeds done for one of the least of his family were done for him; this makes the commentary's minute good deed unexpectedly weighty at final judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b3b18aca12e0c8cd9e64", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.41", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fire assigned to rejected people", "note": "The rejected are sent to eternal fire after the separation; this connects the commentary's inverted patience, doing the works of fire's people, to a final destination."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ae10955e17a667abf05", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.42", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "neglected small acts condemned", "note": "The rejected did not feed the hungry or give drink to the thirsty; this supplies the negative half of the commentary's smallest deed carrying weight at the division."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dfdf93e40795f0144e0b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.44", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rejected people question their verdict", "note": "The rejected ask when they failed to serve the king in his needs; their surprise is a concrete instance of the commentary's people who misjudge the worth of their own conduct."}
{"connection_id": "BC-12e4f2830fe7bb57598a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.46", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "two final destinies", "note": "The commentary's sorting ends in reward or punishment; Matthew closes the sheep-and-goats judgment with eternal punishment for one group and eternal life for the other."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3b9f82ddd8cf5a4d6893", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.46", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "opposed final outcomes", "note": "The passage concludes with punishment for one group and life for the righteous; this matches the commentary's decisive division after the accounting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-17c59fb4bafbe7d5e2f3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.1", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "visible righteousness loses reward", "note": "Jesus warns that righteousness performed to be seen by others receives no reward from the Father; this specifies why work that looks good might fail the commentary's account."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5843e3627923fd8c7dc9", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.21", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing the Father's will", "note": "The commentary's exception includes belief and righteous deeds; Jesus says entry into the kingdom belongs to the one who does the Father's will, distinguishing verbal confession from enacted obedience."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fd4cc4072d6023fba33e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.21", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing the Father's will admits", "note": "Jesus says entry into the kingdom belongs to one doing his Father's will, which explains why the impressive acts claimed in the following verse can still fail the commentary's good-work test."}

