{"connection_id": "BC-bf85cfc245192eca359a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.24.13", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endure to the end", "note": "The commentary's patience belongs to the people who escape loss; Jesus says the one who endures to the end will be saved, placing perseverance within an apocalyptic warning."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bc05ed6407486caf4f5d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.32", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "all nations; separation", "note": "The commentary describes the final distinction between good and evil; Matthew gathers all nations before the Son of Man, who separates people as a shepherd separates sheep from goats."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a6b6755c8fbb45b41cb2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.32", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "separation of all nations", "note": "The Son of Man gathers the nations and separates people as a shepherd separates sheep from goats; this supplies a scene for the commentary's final sorting of good from bad."}
{"connection_id": "BC-41b34f83ffc3f3610d4a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.35", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "concrete deeds rewarded", "note": "The welcomed people fed the hungry and gave drink to the thirsty; the commentary's righteous deeds gain small, tangible instances used in the final verdict."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f058e0c4824acfbe9323", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.40", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "deeds to the least count as deeds to the king", "note": "The commentary says deeds determine the account; Matthew makes acts of care toward the least of the king's siblings count as acts done to the king, giving the judgment criterion a concrete social face."}
{"connection_id": "BC-19a86340046765cf798a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.40", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "act for the least counted for the king", "note": "The king says deeds done for one of the least of his family were done for him; this makes the commentary's minute good deed unexpectedly weighty at final judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b3b18aca12e0c8cd9e64", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.41", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fire assigned to rejected people", "note": "The rejected are sent to eternal fire after the separation; this connects the commentary's inverted patience, doing the works of fire's people, to a final destination."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ae10955e17a667abf05", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.42", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "neglected small acts condemned", "note": "The rejected did not feed the hungry or give drink to the thirsty; this supplies the negative half of the commentary's smallest deed carrying weight at the division."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dfdf93e40795f0144e0b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.44", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rejected people question their verdict", "note": "The rejected ask when they failed to serve the king in his needs; their surprise is a concrete instance of the commentary's people who misjudge the worth of their own conduct."}
{"connection_id": "BC-12e4f2830fe7bb57598a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.46", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "two final destinies", "note": "The commentary's sorting ends in reward or punishment; Matthew closes the sheep-and-goats judgment with eternal punishment for one group and eternal life for the other."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3b9f82ddd8cf5a4d6893", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.25.46", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "opposed final outcomes", "note": "The passage concludes with punishment for one group and life for the righteous; this matches the commentary's decisive division after the accounting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-17c59fb4bafbe7d5e2f3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.1", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "visible righteousness loses reward", "note": "Jesus warns that righteousness performed to be seen by others receives no reward from the Father; this specifies why work that looks good might fail the commentary's account."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5843e3627923fd8c7dc9", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.21", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing the Father's will", "note": "The commentary's exception includes belief and righteous deeds; Jesus says entry into the kingdom belongs to the one who does the Father's will, distinguishing verbal confession from enacted obedience."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fd4cc4072d6023fba33e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.21", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing the Father's will admits", "note": "Jesus says entry into the kingdom belongs to one doing his Father's will, which explains why the impressive acts claimed in the following verse can still fail the commentary's good-work test."}

item.stdout:
{"connection_id": "BC-bedf0228ba2f6e5414b1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.22", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "confident workers appeal to deeds", "note": "Many appeal to prophecy, exorcism, and mighty works done in Jesus' name on that day; this mirrors the commentary's people who think their efforts good before judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a5c9bd0401cdb64b45b5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.23", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "workers of lawlessness rejected", "note": "Jesus rejects those claimants as workers of lawlessness; the commentary likewise says apparent good effort can prove valueless when the actual work is judged."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bfc4e3bc3f7ab683ce58", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.12", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance; commandments; faith", "note": "The commentary's exception joins belief and good action with patience; Revelation identifies the saints by endurance, keeping God's commandments, and faith in Jesus in an apocalyptic judgment setting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a1b37db6ffabf25945d7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.12", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "endurance faith and commands", "note": "The saints' endurance is described as keeping God's commands and faith in Jesus; this places patience, faith, and action together beside the surah's exception."}
{"connection_id": "BC-57422d64a702922d1b0b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.13", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "deeds follow the dead", "note": "The commentary says what people have done is present at judgment; Revelation blesses those who die in the Lord and says their deeds follow them, making work accompany a person beyond death."}
{"connection_id": "BC-17256436da819baa3033", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.13", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "deeds follow the dead", "note": "A voice says those who die in the Lord rest from labors and their works follow them; this closely meets the commentary's time limit, enduring good works, and deeds present afterward."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9daf093417c19576d7a0", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.2.23", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "search hearts and repay works", "note": "The speaker says he searches mind and heart and will give each person according to works; this adds the inward quality of deeds to the commentary's personal final account."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ee73fbfc656d5c5a239", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.20.12", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "dead judged by written deeds", "note": "The commentary says what people did is present at judgment; Revelation shows the dead before the throne, books opened, and judgment according to what is written of their deeds."}
{"connection_id": "BC-46fb0cce14cf0dbbc8ca", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.20.12", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "books opened and works judged", "note": "The dead stand before the throne while books are opened and are judged by what their works record; this joins the commentary's present deeds to its individual ledger and final tribunal."}
{"connection_id": "BC-203b9e552ba4279c36a7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.20.13", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "each judged by works", "note": "Death and Hades yield the dead, who are judged individually according to deeds; the commentary likewise insists each person meets the consequence of his own work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ae5a90d15f181397d184", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.20.15", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "book and lake of fire", "note": "Anyone absent from the book of life is thrown into the lake of fire; this joins the commentary's record and the fire-bound consequence of evil work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3b9e4f1dd53f31a938cb", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.22.12", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "return; recompense; work", "note": "The commentary joins the appointed end to recompense for each person's work; the returning Christ says he brings reward to repay each according to work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1f93ed0ce446b9cd9f5d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.22.12", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "coming soon with recompense", "note": "The coming speaker brings recompense to repay everyone for what each has done; this links the commentary's approaching appointed day to personal reward."}
{"connection_id": "BC-28af0f63cfbadfdc844f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.3.17", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "imagined wealth conceals poverty", "note": "The Laodiceans claim to need nothing but are called poor and exposed; this supplies the commentary's self-mistaken assessment with a striking deficit image."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0cbe83849f1ecc58eea0", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.3.2", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "works found incomplete", "note": "The risen speaker tells Sardis that its works have not been found complete before God; this is a precise counterpart to the commentary's apparently good work that fails the final assessment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5c3e45e193b288b53dd2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.14.12", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "each gives account to God", "note": "The commentary brings each person to a personal reckoning; Paul says each of us will give an account of himself to God, stressing individual answerability within a dispute about judging fellow believers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-52cb2b37ca9edf7a2e5b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.5", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath stored for judgment day", "note": "Paul says a hard heart stores up wrath for the day of righteous judgment; this meets the commentary's accumulated evil and appointed day."}
{"connection_id": "BC-25e92e7e27c4779e2657", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.6", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "repayment according to work", "note": "The commentary says the day brings every person to account by deeds; Paul states that God repays each according to works, applying the rule without a named exception."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9f7026f12646ac9c7098", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.6", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "repayment according to works", "note": "Paul says God repays each person according to works; this precisely matches the commentary's explanation that the day assigns each human a consequence by work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9d0a6fce11e202cf131b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.7", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "perseverance in good work", "note": "The commentary's exception combines righteous work with patience; Paul describes those who persist in good work while seeking glory and honor as receiving eternal life."}

