{"connection_id": "BC-9daa1618fe33c6e3077c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.90.8", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "secret sins exposed", "note": "The commentary says deeds are found present at reckoning; the psalm says God sets iniquities and hidden sins before his face, adding the exposure of what a person conceals."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6e5dc034b2d3c7408395", "ref": "WLC:Ps.90.8", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hidden sins set before God", "note": "The psalm says God sets iniquities and secret sins before him; the commentary likewise says what people did will be present rather than lost from the account."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d7ee5ac358a78791a15e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.98.9", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "world judged in righteousness", "note": "The commentary's accounting concerns every person; the psalm pictures the Lord coming to judge the world and peoples with righteousness and equity, extending judgment to the whole inhabited world."}
{"connection_id": "BC-20501a8a55e4527c18d4", "ref": "WLC:Zech.8.16", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speak truth to one another", "note": "The commentary's mutual urging of truth has a close communal counterpart in Zechariah's command to speak truth to one another and judge with truth and peace in the gates; Zechariah locates this ethic in civic restoration."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a4298a768dbd2d48ae34", "ref": "WLC:Zech.8.16", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "speak truth to neighbor and judge justly", "note": "Zechariah joins truthful speech to one's neighbor with judgments of truth and peace at the gates; this gives the surah's mutual counsel in truth a communal judicial setting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-289fe1c098ebddc70d85", "ref": "WLC:Zeph.2.2", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew חקק in decree; table sound correspondence", "note": "Zephaniah urges action before the decree takes effect and before the Lord's angry day arrives; this places a prescribed term beside the commentary's appointed judgment day, while the root link remains unverified."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d2204adab3c79776ac89", "ref": "Wisdom of Solomon 3:1", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "righteous souls not lost", "note": "The commentary says humanity is in loss except for the faithful who do good; Wisdom says the souls of the righteous are in God's hand and appear untouched by torment, challenging the inference that visible death means final loss."}
{"connection_id": "BC-08a26c1ccd4a7c1e9b52", "ref": "Wisdom of Solomon 3:9", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith; truth; mercy", "note": "The commentary's exception joins belief, righteous action, and truth; Wisdom says those who trust God understand truth and the faithful remain with him in love, grounding the righteous group's future in trust and divine mercy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f7cf6e7e2a319d1dac45", "ref": "Wisdom of Solomon 5:1", "target": "sec13", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "righteous stand boldly at judgment", "note": "The commentary's exception is the group not lost; Wisdom pictures the righteous standing with great confidence before those who oppressed them, adding vindication after apparent defeat."}

