+{"connection_id":"BC-ef8b4e94330bb210f41d","ref":"WLC:Prov.6.32","status":"rejected","reason":"The adulterer is חסר־לב, lacking sense, and destroys himself; its lack is cognitive in an adultery warning, not the weighed loss of Daniel 5:27.","paragraphs":[36],"evidence":["WLC:Prov.6.32"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-df5faf21600d7aea5eaf","ref":"WLC:Ps.1.3","status":"accepted","reason":"צַלח appears as יַצְלִיחַ for all the righteous person's doing; the annotation distinguishes prosperity from morally righteous صالح deeds.","paragraphs":[37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.1.3","WLC:Ps.1.4","WLC:Ps.1.6"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-004"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-260a88298fe30ea990bd","ref":"WLC:Ps.1.3","status":"accepted","reason":"The Torah-rooted person's actions prosper; the adjacent chaff and perishing-way verses sharpen the contrast while the root correspondence remains unverified.","paragraphs":[37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.1.3","WLC:Ps.1.4","WLC:Ps.1.6"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-004"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-53938c2502b9fcef60a4","ref":"WLC:Ps.1.4","status":"accepted","reason":"The wicked are windblown chaff against the fruitful tree of 1:3; this is the annotation's stated counterimage, not a literal scale.","paragraphs":[37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.1.3","WLC:Ps.1.4","WLC:Ps.1.6"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-004"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-481d70ec5a08115acaed","ref":"WLC:Ps.1.6","status":"accepted","reason":"The Lord knows the righteous path while the wicked path perishes, completing Psalm 1's separated outcomes stated in the annotation.","paragraphs":[37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.1.3","WLC:Ps.1.4","WLC:Ps.1.6"],"annotations":["S103-TEV-SYD-004"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-abaec22688645cdc92b4","ref":"WLC:Ps.15.2","status":"rejected","reason":"The temple guest does righteousness and speaks truth inwardly, but does not mutually counsel others or face a weighed final account; Malachi 3:16-18 is closer.","paragraphs":[37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.15.2"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7264994af3075e0ad5e5","ref":"WLC:Ps.34.11","status":"rejected","reason":"Seekers lack no good thing while lions hunger; חסר is present provision, not the final personal deficit in the page's scale.","paragraphs":[36],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.34.11"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-84e02a3e6ae927b4e958","ref":"WLC:Ps.37.7","status":"rejected","reason":"The wicked prosper now while the worshiper waits; this temporary observation does not contradict the commentary's final valuation, and צלח still means prosperity rather than صالح righteousness.","paragraphs":[37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.37.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-87817137238b0d0d630c","ref":"WLC:Ps.39.7","status":"rejected","reason":"A person piles possessions without knowing their eventual recipient; צבר means heap, not Arabic صبر patience, and the page piles wickedness rather than goods.","paragraphs":[36,37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.39.7"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7bccab5684d30ca7fcd8","ref":"WLC:Ps.50.21","status":"rejected","reason":"God threatens to arrange the sinner's acts before his eyes in rebuke, but this is not an opened universal deed book or fixed judgment day like Revelation 20:12.","paragraphs":[37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.50.21"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-e75b4540912c1d3f5711","ref":"WLC:Ps.62.10","status":"rejected","reason":"People, not their deeds, rise as lighter than breath on scales; using this as proof of weighed works would confuse the object being measured.","paragraphs":[36,37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.62.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f43aaa5550e7dc932289","ref":"WLC:Ps.62.10","status":"rejected","reason":"The balances express the insubstantiality of all human ranks, not a good/bad deed count with a righteous exception.","paragraphs":[37],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.62.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d5ea840e11747d530fe6","ref":"WLC:Ps.62.13","status":"rejected","reason":"God repays each according to work, but this adds no new point beyond the selected Romans 2:6 rule; Psalm 62:10's scales weigh people, not these works.","paragraphs":[36],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.62.13"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-420021d518a5c64951f6","ref":"WLC:Ps.62.13","status":"rejected","reason":"The psalm states personal work-based recompense but does not join it to an end-time deed scale; Romans 2:6-8 treats the same rule and alternatives.","paragraphs":[36],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.62.13"],"annotations":[]}

